(Hypertension severity modifies anticoagulation benefit in cryptogenic stroke with atrial) Tj
T*
(cardiopathy: exploratory analysis from the ARCADIA trial) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Background: Disparate trial results in cryptogenic stroke may reflect heterogeneous) Tj
T*
(underlying stroke mechanisms. We examined whether hypertension severity modifies) Tj
T*
(anticoagulation efficacy. Methods: From 945 patients with cryptogenic stroke and atrial) Tj
T*
(cardiopathy randomized to apixaban versus aspirin between 2018 and 2023, we analysed 945) Tj
T*
(with complete hypertension and imaging data. Hypertension with high-risk features) Tj
T*
(\(elevated systolic BP >=160 mmHg and/or ventricular hypertrophy imaging\) was present in 351) Tj
T*
(\(37.1%\) participants. Results: A significant treatment-by-hypertension interaction was) Tj
T*
(observed \(p=0.024\). In 594 patients without high-risk hypertension, apixaban demonstrated) Tj
T*
(superior efficacy \(hazard ratio 0.43; 95% CI 0.22-0.85; absolute risk reduction 3.4% over) Tj
T*
(median 1.6 years\). Conversely, in 351 with hypertension high-risk features, no efficacy) Tj
T*
(difference emerged \(hazard ratio 1.68; 95% CI 0.78-3.62; p=0.19\); absolute event rate) Tj
T*
(difference 2.4% favoured aspirin. Conclusions: Advanced hypertension phenotypes may) Tj
T*
(indicate stroke mechanisms resistant to anticoagulation benefit, possibly reflecting) Tj
T*
(hypertensive arteriolosclerosis rather than cardioembolism. Trial design accounting for) Tj
T*
(hypertension severity may better identify populations deriving anticoagulation benefit in) Tj
T*
(cryptogenic stroke.) Tj
